<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (After more than 40 years in the orthotics and prosthetics profession, Sy Rosen is retiring, leaving behind a legacy of compassion, innovation, and exceptional patient care. Since entering the field in 1982, Sy has been driven by the opportunity to help people regain their independence while solving complex challenges.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (Reflecting on his career, Sy shared that while technology and craftsmanship were important, the most rewarding part of his work was building relationships with patients, earning their trust, and witnessing life-changing moments. Throughout his career, he also built two successful O&P businesses, with Stellar O&P eventually becoming part of the Bionic family.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (When asked what advice he would offer the next generation, Sy emphasized that patient care should always come first. "Never forget that the device is not the patient," he said. He encourages practitioners to listen carefully, continue learning, pay attention to the details, and always treat patients with dignity and respect.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
